/P 161 0 R
/T (Steps of the Program Step 1: Import Scanner import java.util.Scanner; This is used to take input from the keyboard. Step 2: Create the Student class The class contains: studentname rollno s1 s2 s3 total percentage These store the student's information and marks. Step 3: Create studentdetails\(\) This method asks the user to enter: Student name Roll number First subject marks Second subject marks Third subject marks The entered values are stored in the corresponding variables. Step 4: Create calc\(\) This method calculates the total: total = s1 + s2 + s3; Then calculates percentage: percentage = total / 3.00; Step 5: Create show\(\) This method displays: Student name Roll number Subject 1 marks Subject 2 marks Subject 3 marks Total Percentage Step 6: Create StudentProgram The main\(\) method creates a Student object: Student st = new Student\(\); Step 7: Display the menu The program repeatedly displays: 1. Enter student details 2. Calculate total and percentage 3. Show result 4. Exit Step 8: Read the user's choice choice = sp.nextInt\(\); Step 9: Execute the selected option A switch statement handles the choice: Choice Operation 1 Enter student details 2 Calculate total and percentage 3 Show result 4 Exit Other Invalid choice Step 10: Repeat the menu The do-while loop continues until: choice == 4 Step 11: Exit When the user selects 4, the program displays: exited and stops.)
/E (Steps of the Program Step 1: Import Scanner import java.util.Scanner; This is used to take input from the keyboard. Step 2: Create the Student class The class contains: studentname rollno s1 s2 s3 total percentage These store the student's information and marks. Step 3: Create studentdetails\(\) This method asks the user to enter: Student name Roll number First subject marks Second subject marks Third subject marks The entered values are stored in the corresponding variables. Step 4: Create calc\(\) This method calculates the total: total = s1 + s2 + s3; Then calculates percentage: percentage = total / 3.00; Step 5: Create show\(\) This method displays: Student name Roll number Subject 1 marks Subject 2 marks Subject 3 marks Total Percentage Step 6: Create StudentProgram The main\(\) method creates a Student object: Student st = new Student\(\); Step 7: Display the menu The program repeatedly displays: 1. Enter student details 2. Calculate total and percentage 3. Show result 4. Exit Step 8: Read the user's choice choice = sp.nextInt\(\); Step 9: Execute the selected option A switch statement handles the choice: Choice Operation 1 Enter student details 2 Calculate total and percentage 3 Show result 4 Exit Other Invalid choice Step 10: Repeat the menu The do-while loop continues until: choice == 4 Step 11: Exit When the user selects 4, the program displays: exited and stops.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
